00:01:07.507 --> 00:01:10.483
- So, why's it so important
to find your purpose.

00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:11.576
You probably heard this many times.

00:01:11.576 --> 00:01:13.205
You have to find your purpose,

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:14.552
and when you do your life will be amazing.

00:01:14.552 --> 00:01:15.813
Your life will be more palatable.

00:01:15.813 --> 00:01:17.258
Your life will be a richer experience.

00:01:17.258 --> 00:01:19.134
Well, I'd probably encourage
you then finding your purpose

00:01:19.134 --> 00:01:20.863
is ultimately lying to yourself,

00:01:20.863 --> 00:01:22.248
because at some point you're going to die.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.578
The people who you have affected
positively are going to die.

00:01:24.578 --> 00:01:27.590
And even at some point,
the world is going to die.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.915
So, why do we say it's so
important to find your purpose?

00:01:29.915 --> 00:01:31.604
In my opinion, finding your purpose is

00:01:31.604 --> 00:01:33.884
where you find your humanity,
because most people think

00:01:33.884 --> 00:01:35.721
that just by walking around here like this

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:36.911
that they are a human being.

00:01:36.911 --> 00:01:38.855
And technically, biologically,

00:01:38.855 --> 00:01:40.300
that is true, they are human beings.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.743
But philosophically, by
another way of looking at it,

00:01:42.743 --> 00:01:44.677
many of these people are
just a biological mass

00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:46.505
reacting to their environment.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.207
Their values are imposed upon them.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.653
Their opinions are imposed upon them.

00:01:49.653 --> 00:01:51.888
And they walk through life reacting.

00:01:51.888 --> 00:01:54.048
They're soaking in
information like a sponge,

00:01:54.048 --> 00:01:56.082
and there is a lack of a core.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.363
What finding your purpose
does is it creates gravity.

00:01:58.363 --> 00:02:00.587
The gravity of personal boundaries.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.144
When you have a purpose, you
have to create boundaries

00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:05.837
about what you will and will
not allow into your life.

00:02:05.837 --> 00:02:09.220
That's both from other people,
but also your own behavior.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.650
Start now, start immediately,

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.696
start yesterday, start as soon as you can.

00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:15.854
You have these grand plans in your mind,

00:02:15.854 --> 00:02:18.389
this grand vision of how things would look

00:02:18.389 --> 00:02:19.963
when you finally start it.

00:02:19.963 --> 00:02:22.104
Maybe you're thinking of
approaching that first girl,

00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:24.258
or doing that first night of approaching.

00:02:24.258 --> 00:02:26.868
And you think, "If I finally
did that, what would happen?

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.562
"Could I do the perfect first
approach and get married?

00:02:29.562 --> 00:02:30.879
"Could I avoid rejection?

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:33.413
"Could I have my first
night out be my last?"

00:02:33.413 --> 00:02:34.590
It's not going to happen.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.656
Anything that's worth
doing will take time.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.453
It's going to take a lot of work.

00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:39.968
It's going to take a lot of repetition.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.559
This grand vision that
you have in your mind

00:02:41.559 --> 00:02:45.177
of perfection is
interfering with your life.

00:02:45.177 --> 00:02:47.795
Forget perfection, start immediately.

00:02:47.795 --> 00:02:49.835
I remember when I created
The Blueprint program.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.517
And for years I thought,
"If I just put out

00:02:51.517 --> 00:02:53.968
"this one Blueprint program,
my entire life will change."

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:56.223
The Blueprint came out, it made
a couple of million dollars.

00:02:56.223 --> 00:02:58.599
And guess what, I took
that money, sunk it back

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:01.480
into my company, and I was
back in the same place.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.284
The same thing goes for all the best ideas

00:03:03.284 --> 00:03:04.854
that I've ever released on video.

00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:07.027
I thought, "Oh, I'll just put it out,

00:03:07.027 --> 00:03:09.309
"and once it's out it will go viral

00:03:09.309 --> 00:03:12.889
"and disseminate across the
planet and change the world."

00:03:12.889 --> 00:03:14.464
Well, did the world change
when I put out that video?

00:03:14.464 --> 00:03:16.881
No, if I want to change the
world, what will I have to do?

00:03:16.881 --> 00:03:18.703
I will have to grind,
I will have to hustle,

00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:20.616
I will have to keep going and persevering

00:03:20.616 --> 00:03:23.041
for years and maybe decades.

00:03:23.041 --> 00:03:25.232
Whatever it is that you want
to do, start immediately.

00:03:25.232 --> 00:03:27.194
Get over that perfect idea in your mind.

00:03:27.194 --> 00:03:31.168
Start bad, do a bad job,
do a job, make it suck.

00:03:31.168 --> 00:03:33.379
At least you're getting
some momentum with it.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.087
Once you get out there and
you see how much you suck,

00:03:35.087 --> 00:03:36.725
you can begin to make changes,

00:03:36.725 --> 00:03:38.459
you can begin to make adjustments.

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:41.037
And at least, you're taking action.

00:03:41.037 --> 00:03:44.287
Do not wait to start, waiting to start.

00:03:45.293 --> 00:03:47.579
The time to start is now.

00:03:47.579 --> 00:03:50.721
First of all, I believe that most people,

00:03:50.721 --> 00:03:52.982
there's really only a few key areas

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:56.591
where we have almost like a super power.

00:03:56.591 --> 00:03:58.066
Aptitudes, all right, I guess we could

00:03:58.066 --> 00:04:00.095
call it a super aptitude.

00:04:00.095 --> 00:04:02.026
And we're looking for
those super aptitudes

00:04:02.026 --> 00:04:05.348
all the time by trying
out different lanes.

00:04:05.348 --> 00:04:06.950
All right, so take myself.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.271
I'm somebody who has
attention deficit disorder.

00:04:09.271 --> 00:04:12.568
And what that means is that I
can speak almost indefinitely.

00:04:12.568 --> 00:04:15.619
It means that I also have
almost infinite creativity.

00:04:15.619 --> 00:04:17.743
And that also comes from
growing up with depression.

00:04:17.743 --> 00:04:20.041
When you're depressed,
that can oftentimes trigger

00:04:20.041 --> 00:04:22.469
this very, very intense creativity.

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:25.804
So, between having depression,
attention deficit disorder,

00:04:25.804 --> 00:04:27.413
and also in my case, if you look at things

00:04:27.413 --> 00:04:30.140
like growing up unable
to read social cues,

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:31.571
you have an interesting recipe for

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:34.047
how I built Real Social Dynamics.

00:04:34.047 --> 00:04:35.426
So, I basically found my super aptitudes

00:04:35.426 --> 00:04:38.237
because by not understanding
something so thoroughly,

00:04:38.237 --> 00:04:40.993
I had to break it down so
deeply to understand it,

00:04:40.993 --> 00:04:43.502
that's social dynamics,
which creates great content.

00:04:43.502 --> 00:04:45.973
Plus I'm being depressed,
that creates creativity.

00:04:45.973 --> 00:04:48.074
And also having ADD
allows me to talk forever

00:04:48.074 --> 00:04:50.447
because I don't feel the passage of time

00:04:50.447 --> 00:04:51.639
in the way that a normal person does.

00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:54.417
I can't feel time passing,
so I could do this forever.

00:04:54.417 --> 00:04:57.731
Okay, so if you look at that,
that created a super aptitude.

00:04:57.731 --> 00:04:59.167
Now, how did I find it?

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:01.534
I tried out many different things.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.248
As long as I was trying out
different things, I was happy.

00:05:04.248 --> 00:05:06.108
So, tried out one thing,
tried another thing,

00:05:06.108 --> 00:05:07.369
tried another thing, tried another thing,

00:05:07.369 --> 00:05:08.517
tried another thing.

00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:10.679
The enemy of the best is the good.

00:05:10.679 --> 00:05:11.945
So, once you have a pretty good life,

00:05:11.945 --> 00:05:13.487
you're established as a man.

00:05:13.487 --> 00:05:16.456
What's to motivate you to keep
going to that elite level?

00:05:16.456 --> 00:05:17.894
The one that I think is the most powerful

00:05:17.894 --> 00:05:21.314
in the long term, of course,
is higher self-motivation.

00:05:21.314 --> 00:05:23.448
And that's when you've taken
the focus off of yourself

00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:25.503
and you're seeing what
it does for other people.

00:05:25.503 --> 00:05:27.518
Basically, you reach a very
high paradigm where your sense

00:05:27.518 --> 00:05:29.463
of identity is not just tied up in you,

00:05:29.463 --> 00:05:31.672
but in everything that you see around you.

00:05:31.672 --> 00:05:33.785
Okay, you are this, you're this,

00:05:33.785 --> 00:05:34.972
you're part of your environment,

00:05:34.972 --> 00:05:36.600
your environment is a part of you.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.061
And people who you dislike
are just a simple part

00:05:39.061 --> 00:05:42.946
of the elements and the lay of
the land in that environment.

00:05:42.946 --> 00:05:45.549
When you can actually take on,

00:05:45.549 --> 00:05:47.274
I guess you could call it a larger circle

00:05:47.274 --> 00:05:50.324
of concerns, as Stephen
Covey would call it,

00:05:50.324 --> 00:05:52.756
you have a very, very long term

00:05:52.756 --> 00:05:54.147
and very powerful motivation.

00:05:54.147 --> 00:05:55.460
It's the kind of thing that motivates you

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:59.246
to get out in the rain and record a video.

00:05:59.246 --> 00:06:00.989
'Cause you're not doing
it so much for yourself,

00:06:00.989 --> 00:06:02.917
you know, I could be recording
a video like this in a room,

00:06:02.917 --> 00:06:05.115
but just because I want
people to enjoy watching it.

00:06:05.115 --> 00:06:07.153
And I see an opportunity,
boom, I want to do it.

00:06:07.153 --> 00:06:11.055
So, that's the most powerful
motivation in the long term.

00:06:11.055 --> 00:06:13.860
Okay, that's what's going to
make you just go and go and go.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.530
But where's the problem there?

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.142
Well, higher self-motivation is good,

00:06:18.142 --> 00:06:19.635
except what starts to happen is you start

00:06:19.635 --> 00:06:22.517
to ignore things like,
I don't know, marketing.

00:06:22.517 --> 00:06:24.296
You're all up in the skies, man,

00:06:24.296 --> 00:06:26.332
thinking about higher purpose, man.

00:06:26.332 --> 00:06:28.267
And all this kind of, we're all one, man.

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:30.367
And then all of a sudden,
you can't pay your rent

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.308
'cause you didn't do things
the way that you should do it.

00:06:32.308 --> 00:06:33.896
You didn't handle something
simple like marketing.

00:06:33.896 --> 00:06:36.880
Oh, marketing, oh, it's
all so barbaric, right?

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.236
Things like that, and
then you get screwed.

00:06:39.236 --> 00:06:42.671
So, every single motivation is good.

00:06:42.671 --> 00:06:45.303
They're all there to help you.

00:06:45.303 --> 00:06:48.863
Personally for me, why I love
the higher self-motivation

00:06:48.863 --> 00:06:52.361
is because, I don't know, just petty,

00:06:52.361 --> 00:06:54.112
it doesn't do a lot for me at this point.

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:56.158
And day to day practical concerns,

00:06:56.158 --> 00:06:57.444
I've already handled that, right?

00:06:57.444 --> 00:06:58.736
So for me, it's about the higher self.

00:06:58.736 --> 00:07:02.767
But at the same time, I like
to tap into all elements of it.

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:05.167
I'm not above a little
petty fun once in a while.

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:06.834
And I'm definitely not above handling my

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:09.701
day to day concerns as a
man, especially as a father.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:12.253
So again, all motivations are good.

00:07:12.253 --> 00:07:14.745
Be aware of the longevity of each type

00:07:14.745 --> 00:07:16.898
of motivation and then tap into it.

00:07:16.898 --> 00:07:20.275
You think to yourself,
"Why am I so damn needy?

00:07:20.275 --> 00:07:21.748
"I wish I could get rid of this neediness.

00:07:21.748 --> 00:07:24.678
"I wish I could try harder
to become less needy."

00:07:24.678 --> 00:07:26.751
But actually, what I'm
going to suggest to you is

00:07:26.751 --> 00:07:30.983
that rather than trying
harder to eliminate neediness,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:32.922
another focus that you
could take is creating

00:07:32.922 --> 00:07:36.277
what I call an ecosystem
of positive emotions.

00:07:36.277 --> 00:07:39.122
Just like I was saying about
this Hamilton Pool right here,

00:07:39.122 --> 00:07:41.155
you have to learn to nurture yourself.

00:07:41.155 --> 00:07:43.971
You have to learn to fill your own cup.

00:07:43.971 --> 00:07:44.847
Okay, so this is very similar

00:07:44.847 --> 00:07:47.100
to something like say, time management.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.074
Let's say that you're late all the time,

00:07:48.074 --> 00:07:52.652
and you think, "I have to
try harder to be on time.

00:07:52.652 --> 00:07:54.019
"I've got to try harder."

00:07:54.019 --> 00:07:56.617
And you try harder, you
try harder, you try harder.

00:07:56.617 --> 00:07:57.950
And maybe even people will say to you,

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.608
"Hey man, if you're late all the time,

00:07:59.608 --> 00:08:01.596
"it shows that you disrespect
other people's time.

00:08:01.596 --> 00:08:02.870
"You're a disrespectful person."

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.227
And you hear that and you
think, "Wow, I know that.

00:08:05.227 --> 00:08:07.728
"I don't want to be disrespectful
to other people's time."

00:08:07.728 --> 00:08:10.441
But what you're not realizing
that by trying harder,

00:08:10.441 --> 00:08:11.946
you're not going to fix the problem.

00:08:11.946 --> 00:08:13.777
If you're somebody who's naturally late,

00:08:13.777 --> 00:08:15.418
the thing you have to
do is find other people

00:08:15.418 --> 00:08:17.158
to help you to be on time,
or you have to set alarms,

00:08:17.158 --> 00:08:19.205
or set multiple alarms,
or put little tripwires

00:08:19.205 --> 00:08:21.353
around your house, or
find literal processes

00:08:21.353 --> 00:08:22.734
that you can bring to the equation

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:24.480
that will stop you from being late.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.434
Well, it's the same thing that goes

00:08:25.434 --> 00:08:26.665
for stopping being needy.

00:08:26.665 --> 00:08:28.399
So, you might tell yourself,

00:08:28.399 --> 00:08:30.699
"I have to try harder not to be needy."

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:34.751
And you can do that, and much
like stopping being late,

00:08:34.751 --> 00:08:35.989
you can have a bit of success with that.

00:08:35.989 --> 00:08:36.973
But what I would suggest to you is

00:08:36.973 --> 00:08:39.963
that you need to actually
build a different way

00:08:39.963 --> 00:08:42.818
of looking at it to stop being needy.

00:08:42.818 --> 00:08:45.651
(water splashing)

00:08:54.646 --> 00:08:55.793
You have one foot in one reality,

00:08:55.793 --> 00:08:57.005
and one foot in another reality.

00:08:57.005 --> 00:08:59.043
You try to keep one foot in the presence,

00:08:59.043 --> 00:09:00.740
realizing the world's perfect as it is,

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.167
and the other side is the desire to fight.

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:06.688
And to fight the bull that you
see happening in the world.

00:09:06.688 --> 00:09:10.855
To fight the mediocrity and
complacency and just sucking.

00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:16.966
I know for me, one of
my biggest questions is,

00:09:18.128 --> 00:09:19.331
when I think of the
pain that I went through

00:09:19.331 --> 00:09:21.816
for my first couple of decades.

00:09:21.816 --> 00:09:24.909
That was so painful that
that left an imprint

00:09:24.909 --> 00:09:29.133
on me permanently that for
me to not spend my life,

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.678
like given the
opportunities that I've had,

00:09:30.678 --> 00:09:33.232
and to even things that
looked like negative luck,

00:09:33.232 --> 00:09:34.892
in reality, gave me
sort of motivations that

00:09:34.892 --> 00:09:36.273
in the end wound up as opportunities.

00:09:36.273 --> 00:09:38.136
So, you could argue that
I had a very hard life,

00:09:38.136 --> 00:09:40.862
but those things that were hard resulted

00:09:40.862 --> 00:09:42.695
in where I'm at today.

00:09:43.995 --> 00:09:47.495
For me not to spend my whole life fighting

00:09:49.068 --> 00:09:51.818
for the outcome of helping people

00:09:54.201 --> 00:09:55.385
to have a path forward to get out

00:09:55.385 --> 00:09:57.633
of the reality that I was in,

00:09:57.633 --> 00:10:01.064
I would have to acknowledge
that my life has no value.

00:10:01.064 --> 00:10:03.022
Like if that makes sense.

00:10:03.022 --> 00:10:05.767
For me to say, "You know
what, I got out of that bull,

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:08.608
that mental cloud of hell
that I was in, growing up.

00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:10.304
I found pathways out of it,

00:10:10.304 --> 00:10:11.874
and I'm not going to spend
my life showing other people

00:10:11.874 --> 00:10:14.584
those pathways that I personally learned.

00:10:14.584 --> 00:10:16.749
I'd have to say that would
basically be me having to say,

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:19.142
"You know what, there's really
no point to life anyway.

00:10:19.142 --> 00:10:20.509
"There's no point to humanity.

00:10:20.509 --> 00:10:22.179
"So, I might as well just have fun."

00:10:22.179 --> 00:10:27.048
And that may be the truth. (laughing)

00:10:27.048 --> 00:10:31.066
It's just a big narcissistic
self-involved exercise.

00:10:31.066 --> 00:10:33.306
But I've made the choice
to value human life,

00:10:33.306 --> 00:10:36.348
and I've made the choice to
fight as hard as I can for that.

00:10:36.348 --> 00:10:39.372
And so, ultimately for
me, I think the decision

00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:41.431
that I've made is like happiness to me,

00:10:41.431 --> 00:10:44.625
like when I'm happiest, is
when I'm pushing towards that.

00:10:44.625 --> 00:10:46.167
And taking time off is nice

00:10:46.167 --> 00:10:49.350
if it's to recharge to go back to the war.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:51.142
And war doesn't mean necessarily fighting

00:10:51.142 --> 00:10:54.210
against something, but
fighting for something,

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.892
like just fighting for
that positive outcome.

00:10:55.892 --> 00:10:57.303
So, don't think of it as a war,

00:10:57.303 --> 00:10:58.136
'cause in a certain way, I'm thinking

00:10:58.136 --> 00:10:59.690
whenever you're fighting
against something,

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:01.342
like they say, "Whatever
you resist, persists."

00:11:01.342 --> 00:11:03.077
So, it's not like that kind of resistance.

00:11:03.077 --> 00:11:04.621
You don't want to bring
resistance into it,

00:11:04.621 --> 00:11:05.560
that's what I was talking about earlier.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.507
You don't want to bring
resistance against something

00:11:07.507 --> 00:11:10.872
into your war, but you want
to just think of a happier,

00:11:10.872 --> 00:11:13.459
more kind of present energy based outcome

00:11:13.459 --> 00:11:17.141
and push towards that, you
just push towards that.

00:11:17.141 --> 00:11:18.877
And use all of your faculties.

00:11:18.877 --> 00:11:21.983
Every faculty that you
have, honing it internally

00:11:21.983 --> 00:11:23.460
and externally honing it, honing it,

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.127
honing it to get it to that level,

00:11:25.127 --> 00:11:26.786
and just continually sharpening the sword.

00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:29.116
The inner sword but also
your outer abilities,

00:11:29.116 --> 00:11:30.048
just sharpening it.

00:11:30.048 --> 00:11:31.576
And that's life for me.

00:11:31.576 --> 00:11:34.087
What I want you to do is I want
you to think of your brain,

00:11:34.087 --> 00:11:36.527
not like you're actually
in control of your brain,

00:11:36.527 --> 00:11:37.610
but actually rather think of your brain

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:40.242
like a stubborn horse
or a stubborn elephant.

00:11:40.242 --> 00:11:41.075
And I want you to take on

00:11:41.075 --> 00:11:43.723
what I call the chariot riding frame.

00:11:43.723 --> 00:11:46.436
And what that means is that
a guy who's going to pick up,

00:11:46.436 --> 00:11:47.827
it's like the charioteer,

00:11:47.827 --> 00:11:49.718
he's going to smack it on the horse.

00:11:49.718 --> 00:11:51.735
And what happens as a result of that is

00:11:51.735 --> 00:11:54.281
that you have to learn
it coaxing the horse

00:11:54.281 --> 00:11:56.438
to go to where you want it to go.

00:11:56.438 --> 00:11:58.025
So, let's say that I'm going
to come out on the coldest day

00:11:58.025 --> 00:11:59.273
of the year to record a video blog.

00:11:59.273 --> 00:12:00.993
I say to myself, "You know
what, I'll just show up

00:12:00.993 --> 00:12:02.757
"and we'll see if I
like it, if I can do it.

00:12:02.757 --> 00:12:04.500
"And I can always go home
if I want to go home."

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.614
And once I'm out here,
it's like, who gives a.

00:12:06.614 --> 00:12:07.642
I should start to have fun with it.

00:12:07.642 --> 00:12:09.024
It's kind of frightening,
I feel like I'm literally

00:12:09.024 --> 00:12:11.441
about to die, but we'll wrap this quickly.

00:12:11.441 --> 00:12:13.251
Likewise, say I'm going to go to the gym

00:12:13.251 --> 00:12:14.242
and I'm not feeling well.

00:12:14.242 --> 00:12:15.658
Maybe I'll just say, "You know what, dude,

00:12:15.658 --> 00:12:16.824
"I'll just warm up."

00:12:16.824 --> 00:12:20.378
And if I could just warm
up then good enough.

00:12:20.378 --> 00:12:22.505
Once I get there, I'll
probably take action, right?

00:12:22.505 --> 00:12:24.043
So, that's fine.

00:12:24.043 --> 00:12:25.603
How about if it's with homework?

00:12:25.603 --> 00:12:26.436
Okay, I'll just read a page

00:12:26.436 --> 00:12:27.957
or I'll just go do one math problem.

00:12:27.957 --> 00:12:29.560
Next thing you know,
you're crackin' into it.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.835
Well, whenever you get into a venue,

00:12:31.835 --> 00:12:32.993
I want you to think of it the same way.

00:12:32.993 --> 00:12:34.844
Like look, I'm just going
to go do a quick approach.

00:12:34.844 --> 00:12:35.872
I'm just going to say hi.

00:12:35.872 --> 00:12:39.926
Even on the way to the
venue, just start saying hi.

00:12:39.926 --> 00:12:41.609
Literally, that's what
I suggest you should do.

00:12:41.609 --> 00:12:42.668
I'm going to send my cameraman inside.

00:12:42.668 --> 00:12:45.597
You, just go inside,
just go, I'm very safe.

00:12:45.597 --> 00:12:48.159
Take the backpack, and you just go inside

00:12:48.159 --> 00:12:51.360
and I will survive here,
and this and this, bang.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:52.456
You've got to become the master

00:12:52.456 --> 00:12:55.161
at coaxing the stubborn horse.

00:12:55.161 --> 00:12:56.530
Literally, you're just the master

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:58.296
at coaxing the stubborn horse.

00:12:58.296 --> 00:13:01.715
And when you have that down, you'll crush.

00:13:01.715 --> 00:13:04.649
But when you can't control the
horse, the horse gets antsy,

00:13:04.649 --> 00:13:08.301
the horse starts making
excuses, and everything goes to.

00:13:08.301 --> 00:13:09.517
Some of the things that I do, for example,

00:13:09.517 --> 00:13:12.355
is right when I get it I'm like, "Hey!"

00:13:12.355 --> 00:13:14.079
And then my reticular activation system

00:13:14.079 --> 00:13:17.127
will see everyone looking at
me, and I'll start scanning.

00:13:17.127 --> 00:13:19.027
I'm like, are people getting
mad, are people getting mad?

00:13:19.027 --> 00:13:21.191
And when I see that nobody's getting mad,

00:13:21.191 --> 00:13:22.435
I realize, you know what?

00:13:22.435 --> 00:13:24.618
I'm not under any kind of threat here.

00:13:24.618 --> 00:13:25.941
And then I go and I crush it.

00:13:25.941 --> 00:13:27.952
So basically, you want to think of it

00:13:27.952 --> 00:13:30.243
like you're always showing your brain

00:13:30.243 --> 00:13:32.918
what I call proof, not promises,

00:13:32.918 --> 00:13:34.574
that nothing bad will happen.

00:13:34.574 --> 00:13:36.592
You just keep fueling
your brain with that.

00:13:36.592 --> 00:13:38.621
So, let's say that you just
go start talking to people.

00:13:38.621 --> 00:13:42.304
Let's just say I talked
to this person here.

00:13:42.304 --> 00:13:43.919
My brain goes, oh, nothing bad happened.

00:13:43.919 --> 00:13:45.815
No one came and attacked
me, it doesn't mean.

00:13:45.815 --> 00:13:47.443
So, you actually lose your status anxiety

00:13:47.443 --> 00:13:48.926
in that environment, and your brain

00:13:48.926 --> 00:13:50.932
will actually unstifle itself.

00:13:50.932 --> 00:13:52.629
So, you want to be constantly coaxing

00:13:52.629 --> 00:13:55.356
your brain into unstifling itself.

00:13:55.356 --> 00:13:56.978
And basically, that's kind of

00:13:56.978 --> 00:13:58.105
the biggest trick I use to warm up.

00:13:58.105 --> 00:13:59.836
I'm just like, hey, I'm
just riding the charioteer,

00:13:59.836 --> 00:14:01.360
or I'm just a charioteer
riding the chariot.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.669
My brain's kind of freezin' now.

00:14:02.669 --> 00:14:04.634
It is very, very difficult
to read something

00:14:04.634 --> 00:14:08.212
that unconsciously or
consciously you know is not going

00:14:08.212 --> 00:14:09.587
to make a big difference in your life.

00:14:09.587 --> 00:14:12.428
You have to believe that it's
going to make the difference.

00:14:12.428 --> 00:14:13.991
You have to see how on your journey,

00:14:13.991 --> 00:14:15.304
it's going to make the difference.

00:14:15.304 --> 00:14:16.875
You need a sense of urgency.

00:14:16.875 --> 00:14:18.157
You need your mind to focus.

00:14:18.157 --> 00:14:19.845
You need to be engaged.

00:14:19.845 --> 00:14:21.807
For someone like me, my
mind doesn't get engaged

00:14:21.807 --> 00:14:24.370
unless I'm stimulated, unless
there's something going on

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.064
in my life that's interesting,
something powerful

00:14:26.064 --> 00:14:28.667
that's going on that's going to
stimulate me to get me engaged.

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:30.772
And this is why every
single time on my journey,

00:14:30.772 --> 00:14:33.042
I encounter some new book or
some new person to learn from.

00:14:33.042 --> 00:14:34.373
I'm loving it.

00:14:34.373 --> 00:14:36.000
You ever notice when I'm
talking about books I'm reading,

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.400
or people I'm learning from,
I'm really all about it?

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.012
That's because there's
something on my journey

00:14:40.012 --> 00:14:42.138
that made me become all about it.

00:14:42.138 --> 00:14:44.494
I'm psyched about it, I'm pumped up.

00:14:44.494 --> 00:14:45.698
Now, another factor to this,

00:14:45.698 --> 00:14:47.330
aside from that sense of urgency,

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.450
is the belief that you can actually do it.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.181
The belief that you actually
can produce a result.

00:14:52.181 --> 00:14:53.952
Take, for example, terrorism.

00:14:53.952 --> 00:14:55.738
Okay, touchy subject, I know.

00:14:55.738 --> 00:14:57.904
Why is it that the best recruits

00:14:57.904 --> 00:15:00.745
for terrorism is people from countries

00:15:00.745 --> 00:15:02.390
where there's a lot of hopelessness?

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:03.620
Well, if there's a lot of hopelessness,

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.970
and you tell somebody,
look, you can go fight

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.587
this big war against these big bad guys,

00:15:07.587 --> 00:15:09.175
say they're going to do something bad

00:15:09.175 --> 00:15:10.859
to this bridge or some crap like that,

00:15:10.859 --> 00:15:12.814
something completely stupid.

00:15:12.814 --> 00:15:14.740
But you tell this person
from a hopeless country,

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.424
you know, you can go on
this grand adventure,

00:15:16.424 --> 00:15:18.784
and take down these bad
people, and da da da.

00:15:18.784 --> 00:15:21.434
And whatever good things
are going to happen

00:15:21.434 --> 00:15:23.193
to you in the afterlife or whatever it is.

00:15:23.193 --> 00:15:25.198
And that person's coming
from a hopeless place,

00:15:25.198 --> 00:15:26.439
the question that I would ask you is

00:15:26.439 --> 00:15:28.620
why wouldn't he do that?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.562
I'm not saying that he should,

00:15:29.562 --> 00:15:31.297
but I'd ask you, why wouldn't he?

00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:32.672
If his life is completely hopeless,

00:15:32.672 --> 00:15:33.772
there's nothing good going on,

00:15:33.772 --> 00:15:35.761
this suddenly starts
providing to a lot of needs

00:15:35.761 --> 00:15:38.066
that person has, and that's
why they take that path.

00:15:38.066 --> 00:15:40.181
That's why if you want to
get rid of terrorism forever,

00:15:40.181 --> 00:15:42.913
killing them all could
maybe be a good approach.

00:15:42.913 --> 00:15:44.924
But an even better approach
if it was possible,

00:15:44.924 --> 00:15:46.826
would actually be to
eliminate hopelessness.

00:15:46.826 --> 00:15:48.325
That would be the best way
to eliminate terrorism,

00:15:48.325 --> 00:15:50.644
in my personal view, but you
may have your own view on that.

00:15:50.644 --> 00:15:51.997
And I'm not an authority on that,

00:15:51.997 --> 00:15:53.816
but that's just a thought
that I have, okay?

00:15:53.816 --> 00:15:55.298
Now, how about as far as believing

00:15:55.298 --> 00:15:56.786
that something is possible?

00:15:56.786 --> 00:16:00.992
Well, take myself, it is
very easy for me to eat kale,

00:16:00.992 --> 00:16:03.878
broccoli, spinach, essential fats,

00:16:03.878 --> 00:16:06.463
clean meats, stuff like that every day.

00:16:06.463 --> 00:16:08.946
It's very easy for me not
to eat processed foods.

00:16:08.946 --> 00:16:10.804
It's very easy for me to go out every day

00:16:10.804 --> 00:16:11.704
and work on my game.

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:13.597
It's very easy for me to
spend a lot of time reading.

00:16:13.597 --> 00:16:15.959
It's very easy for me to do
20 minutes of meditation.

00:16:15.959 --> 00:16:17.565
It's very easy for me that
when people I work with

00:16:17.565 --> 00:16:19.590
are pissing me off, to keep myself calm,

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:22.159
call them calmly and work it
out, all those kinds of things.

00:16:22.159 --> 00:16:23.893
It's very easy for me to do that.

00:16:23.893 --> 00:16:24.726
Do you understand?

00:16:24.726 --> 00:16:25.951
All those things that
people struggle with,

00:16:25.951 --> 00:16:27.363
such as reading a lot, or learning a lot,

00:16:27.363 --> 00:16:28.883
or internalizing it, or implementing it,

00:16:28.883 --> 00:16:30.239
is very easy for me.

00:16:30.239 --> 00:16:31.399
Why?

00:16:31.399 --> 00:16:32.750
The reason that it's easy for me is

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.408
because I believe it's possible.

00:16:35.408 --> 00:16:38.419
I believe that if I do those
things, I will have a payoff.

00:16:38.419 --> 00:16:41.040
So, if you think about a hopeless place,

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:42.643
well, you put a book in front of them,

00:16:42.643 --> 00:16:44.361
you say, "Here look,
learn from this book."

00:16:44.361 --> 00:16:45.379
Why would they read it?

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:46.821
Why would they read it?

00:16:46.821 --> 00:16:49.072
If you don't have the
belief that it's actually

00:16:49.072 --> 00:16:51.678
going to give you a
payoff, there is no point.

00:16:51.678 --> 00:16:53.423
People talk about self-development
and pay lip service

00:16:53.423 --> 00:16:55.862
to it, like you should step
up, man, and things like that.

00:16:55.862 --> 00:16:57.215
But in my experience, stepping up

00:16:57.215 --> 00:16:59.391
in developing yourself involves a lot

00:16:59.391 --> 00:17:01.759
of great wins, and thrills and euphoria.

00:17:01.759 --> 00:17:03.390
But it also involves
a lot of harsh looking

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.009
at yourself, like really
looking at yourself

00:17:05.009 --> 00:17:06.691
in the mirror and questioning yourself.

00:17:06.691 --> 00:17:09.609
You want to believe I'm
awesome and feel your certainty

00:17:09.609 --> 00:17:12.004
and go hard, but I
think that you also want

00:17:12.004 --> 00:17:15.056
to take very, very
harsh looks at yourself.

00:17:15.056 --> 00:17:17.795
That can be very painful and
you want to do that at times.

00:17:17.795 --> 00:17:20.710
And you want to get out into
nature, or into isolation,

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.529
or out with your friends
that will challenge you,

00:17:22.529 --> 00:17:24.613
and think about who you are,

00:17:24.613 --> 00:17:26.295
where you're going, what you become.

00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:28.491
Because again, you're motoring along

00:17:28.491 --> 00:17:30.350
and if you go a little bit this
way, you wind up over here,

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.701
if you're a little bit this
way, you wind up up here,

00:17:31.701 --> 00:17:33.117
if you're a little bit this
way, you wind up over here.

00:17:33.117 --> 00:17:35.187
So, you need those periods of examination

00:17:35.187 --> 00:17:36.736
and kind of pulling out
and looking at that.

00:17:36.736 --> 00:17:39.912
Sometimes I just feel confused.

00:17:39.912 --> 00:17:43.827
I have been reading like
the front page of Roc Nation

00:17:43.827 --> 00:17:46.444
almost every single
day for several months.

00:17:46.444 --> 00:17:48.834
And I'm watching all these videos,

00:17:48.834 --> 00:17:52.283
some of which even
contain different opinions

00:17:52.283 --> 00:17:55.840
on the same topic, and different
angles on the same topic.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:59.423
And I have all this
information in my head.

00:18:00.974 --> 00:18:04.762
Finally, after a couple of
months of not going out,

00:18:04.762 --> 00:18:06.951
and just watching all these videos,

00:18:06.951 --> 00:18:09.546
I walked up to a girl and I have

00:18:09.546 --> 00:18:12.181
all these different ideas in my head.

00:18:12.181 --> 00:18:15.974
And I hear them all at the same time.

00:18:15.974 --> 00:18:18.270
And they're just confusing me.

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:22.779
And I walk up to the girl,
and one guy is telling me

00:18:22.779 --> 00:18:24.612
to be really direct with her.

00:18:24.612 --> 00:18:26.706
Another guy is saying to be funny.

00:18:26.706 --> 00:18:29.190
And another guy's saying I
need to make all this drama

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.191
with her and make her
cry, or call her a dog.

00:18:32.191 --> 00:18:34.225
And another guy is saying just be cool,

00:18:34.225 --> 00:18:35.943
and to be friendly and cool.

00:18:35.943 --> 00:18:38.788
And all these voices and
I hear them in my head,

00:18:38.788 --> 00:18:39.984
and I don't know what to do.

00:18:39.984 --> 00:18:42.905
It's like all these things in my head,

00:18:42.905 --> 00:18:45.132
in my head, just going on.

00:18:45.132 --> 00:18:46.632
And then I just go

00:18:48.457 --> 00:18:50.115
hi,

00:18:50.115 --> 00:18:51.223
hi,

00:18:51.223 --> 00:18:52.131
hi,

00:18:52.131 --> 00:18:53.547
hi,

00:18:53.547 --> 00:18:54.664
hi,

00:18:54.664 --> 00:18:56.331
and then I run away.

00:18:59.339 --> 00:19:04.001
And then sometimes I feel like
I'm just being manipulated

00:19:04.001 --> 00:19:08.524
with all this free content
given to me by these guys,

00:19:08.524 --> 00:19:10.556
and I don't know what to do.

00:19:10.556 --> 00:19:13.635
And I just thought maybe
somebody could help.

00:19:13.635 --> 00:19:16.552
But you know what? Nobody can help.

00:19:18.746 --> 00:19:23.603
It's just meant to manipulate
me and ruin my life.

00:19:23.603 --> 00:19:24.587
Yes, I don't want to jump.

00:19:24.587 --> 00:19:25.650
- Wait a minute, man, don't jump.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.447
It's not worth it, it's not worth it.

00:19:27.447 --> 00:19:31.481
- [Owen] Oh, I'm confused, I'm confused.

00:19:31.481 --> 00:19:33.648
(screams)

00:19:36.394 --> 00:19:37.685
- Thank you, guys, so much for watching.

