I'm really curious to find
out what you have to say.

00:19:58.604 --> 00:20:00.433
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Roger Pierce.

00:20:00.433 --> 00:20:02.967
Roger, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:20:02.967 --> 00:20:05.874
Your One Word, and making that
awesome little cartoon cel

00:20:05.874 --> 00:20:08.358
to start up around my book, as well.

00:20:08.358 --> 00:20:09.896
Thank you so much for the support, man,

00:20:09.896 --> 00:20:11.415
and I hope you enjoy your reading.

00:20:11.415 --> 00:20:13.013
Thank you, guys, so much for watching.

00:20:13.013 --> 00:20:14.756
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:20:14.756 --> 00:20:16.077
to believe in yourself.

00:20:16.077 --> 00:20:18.506
And whatever your one word is,

00:20:18.506 --> 00:20:20.923
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:20:27.056 --> 00:20:28.485
- When you learn to relate to yourself,

00:20:28.485 --> 00:20:32.652
again you have these like low
self-image or bad self-talk.

00:20:33.831 --> 00:20:38.489
Again, a lot of that is
just burning away the bull.

00:20:38.489 --> 00:20:41.579
Guys are like, I can't stop
having these limiting beliefs.

00:20:41.579 --> 00:20:43.154
Or, I can't stop feeling bad about myself.

00:20:43.154 --> 00:20:46.955
It's like, you can, you
have to slowly do it.

00:20:46.955 --> 00:20:48.775
You have to slowly build it up.

00:20:48.775 --> 00:20:53.367
Positivity is a muscle
that you slowly build up,

00:20:53.367 --> 00:20:55.762
and you build them up.

00:20:55.762 --> 00:20:57.558
That's the same kind of thing, right,

00:20:57.558 --> 00:20:58.909
is you have to throw
yourself into the fire

00:20:58.909 --> 00:21:01.347
at the next paradigm until you become

00:21:01.347 --> 00:21:03.672
the person who you want to be.

